iption":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098082,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwODI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gdscript","name":"topic:gdscript","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2025-04-28T16:26:23Z","updated_at":"2025-04-28T16:32:41Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.4.1.stable.steam [49a5bc7b6]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable (49a5bc7b6) - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Mobile) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6094) - AMD Ryzen 5 3600 6-Core Processor (12 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nAs said in the title, Vector types are supported by PROPERTY_HINT_RANGE but can not be used with the much simpler to use @export_range, since Vector types are supported by PROPERTY_HINT_RANGE I don't see why they wouldn't or shouldn't be supported by the @export_range annotation.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a022d259-f440-4f83-a8e2-9561fdc09e53)\n```gdscript\n@export_range(0,100,1.0,\"suffix:%\") var VectorA : Vector2\n@export_custom(PROPERTY_HINT_RANGE, \"0,100,1.0,suffix:%\") var VectorB : Vector2\n```","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105875/reactions","total_count":10,"+1":10,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105875/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}